{
  "title": "Scrape jobs: no timeout or cancel for a step that hangs",
  "description": "A job stuck inside a step stays non-terminal until the server restarts; the only recovery is resume_interrupted_jobs at startup (scraping/runner.rs:279-327). \
There is no cancelled or timed-out state. \
Clients wait on it: the web ImportPage polls for up to SCRAPE_JOB_LONG_POLL_TIMEOUT_MS (10 min) and the iOS text-import loop has no deadline at all (RecipeFormViewModel.swift:125-173). \
BulkReNormalizeModal.pollRows (123-156) has no timeout and swallows every error. \
Want: a per-step deadline that moves the job to failed with a clear error (retryable), and client handling of that failure. \
Pick deadlines per step (AI steps are slow); ask the owner if unsure. \
Found in the 2026-11-07 implicit-state-machine audit; line numbers are as of e94669d4ca, so re-check each point before fixing.",
